{"text": "DEPARTMENT OF THE ARMY\n\u2018502d MILITARY POLICE BN (CID)\n30 MILITARY POLICE GRP (CID)\n2745 KENTUCKY AVE\nFORT CAMPBELL, KY 42223\n\nCIRC-CZA 16 July 2020\n\nMEMORANDUM FOR RECORD.\n\nSUBJECT: Clearview Al, Sole-Source\n\n1. The 502D MP BN Criminal Intelligence Section requires the purchase of 15\nClearview facial recognition software licenses.\n\n2. Clearview Al provides a unique and innovative capability with regard to facial\n\nrecognition technology and its use by law enforcement organizations. The 502d MP\nBN (CID) has been using this tool on a trial basis and has seen an increase of 15%-\n25% success in positively identifying potential subject, victims and witnesses in\npossible crimes under Army CID jusridiction. They were the only company capable of\nproviding the service. Clearview Al is the only service that provides image-based\n\u2018searches of publicly available material, instant links to publicly available online\nwebsites based on the results of their image-based searches and the ability to\n\u2018Manage data inside the system in order to easily catalog investigative products in a_\n\u2018case. While these capabilities may be individually available from other vendors, they\nare not available in combination from any other vendor and without significant\nduplication of cost.\n\nhh\n\nLead Investigative Analyst",
